# Information Disclosure - Exposed Git Repository Leading to Credential Disclosure

## Executive Summary

An information disclosure vulnerability was identified due to the exposure of the application's Git repository through the web server.

The `.git` directory was publicly accessible, allowing an attacker to download the repository metadata and inspect its commit history. Analysis of previous commits revealed that an administrator password had been removed from a configuration file and replaced with an environment variable.

Although the password was no longer present in the latest version of the source code, Git retained the complete history, allowing recovery of the original hardcoded credential.

Using the disclosed password, an attacker could authenticate as the administrator and perform privileged administrative actions.

